WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:06.990
D-181 was used to being picked as a test subject
for the various dangerous and downright terrifying

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:12.690
experiments and lab work the SCP Foundation
had him perform at Secure Facility Site-32.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:19.070
He’d been working for the organization for
nearly 5 years, and he considered every day

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:24.199
he was alive a blessing, and you would too
if you were a D-Class personnel.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:29.579
While no one’s too sure on the exact methods
the SCP Foundation uses to recruit its D-Class

00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:35.440
personnel, there are a few prevalent rumors,
most of which you’ve surely heard before.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.620
Death row prisoners taken into custody by
the Foundation to be unwilling lab rats, ordinary

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:46.350
people that society wouldn’t miss that were
kidnapped off the streets, or sometimes just

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:51.059
volunteers, though we’re not sure who in
their right mind would willingly volunteer

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:56.199
for one of the most degrading, dangerous positions
in the entire Foundation.

00:00:56.199 --> 00:01:00.980
The truth about D-Class is that every site
does it differently, and the Foundation is

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:06.500
well aware of the controversy among its personnel
that comes with recruiting and using D-Class

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:07.500
personnel.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.050
Heck, some sites don’t even have D-Class,
citing their use as inhumane.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:19.200
But at Site-32, things were ordinary, and
D-181 was one of the many D-Class personnel

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.880
drafted into the Foundation via the United
States prison system.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:30.380
Day in and day out, D-181 would have to perform
tests and experiments, most of which he knew

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.320
next to nothing about.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:38.979
Thankfully for him, D-181 had two benefits
that made his stay at Site-32 a little easier.

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:42.890
First, there was the fact that Site-32 was
a low-priority facility.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:48.360
It was located far away from any major population
centers, and overall lacked the expensive

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.790
funding some of the larger sites had.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:55.229
The anomalies contained there were still pretty
dangerous, but due to the lack of available

00:01:55.229 --> 00:02:00.550
funding, most of what the Foundation was able
to afford at Site-32 was regulated to safe

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.329
and euclid-class objects.

00:02:02.329 --> 00:02:07.869
Now, as we all know, object class has nothing
to do with danger levels, and instead is based

00:02:07.869 --> 00:02:12.720
on the difficulty the Foundation has containing
a certain object more than anything else.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.420
So, when a site, such as Site-32 is under-funded
due to being less of a priority to the larger

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:23.010
organization, they’re typically only going
to be containing the bare-minimum in terms

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:24.550
of expenses.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:30.730
That means less expensive containment, and
less elaborate objects for D-181 to work with.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:36.040
It wasn’t a guarantee of safety, as nothing
ever is in the SCP Foundation, but it was

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:41.230
at least beneficial to have an understanding
of what’s going on in the various experiments

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.780
D-181 had to perform throughout the day.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.849
The second thing D-181 appreciated about Site-32
was a little less conventional.

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:53.290
The entire facility was staffed by women,
with the exception of male personnel being

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.489
used for testing purposes.

00:02:55.489 --> 00:03:00.610
The reason for this is due to a very specific
detail about today’s anomaly, which we’ll

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:05.010
get back to, but it was something that D-181
never took for granted.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:10.400
Of course, D-181 was an absolute buffoon when
it came to dating and relations between testing

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:14.959
subjects and researchers were discouraged
and in some cases forbidden.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:20.000
However, he never gave up hope that he might
be able to now find a girlfriend while living

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.290
in a building that was less than 1 percent
male in population.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:28.700
It's important that we state that D-181 was
always respectful to women and never stepped

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:33.810
out of line, which as far as D-Class go, makes
him top tier boyfriend material.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:38.799
Maybe there’s hope for him some day, so
long as he survives the deadly, daily grind

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:41.420
of being on the lowest rung of the Foundation.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:46.780
While those two things kept D-181 as happy
as someone could be while essentially being

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:52.210
enslaved to the Foundation, there was a lot
to be unhappy about in his position.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:57.250
First, there was the general danger that came
with testing with anomalies every day, where

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:02.739
anything and everything could go wrong, and
your safety was never guaranteed.

00:04:02.739 --> 00:04:05.409
Then, there were the dreams.

00:04:05.409 --> 00:04:10.659
Most of the time, D-181’s waking state felt
like a dream, so that meant the images his

00:04:10.659 --> 00:04:14.040
brain showed him at night were extra weird.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:19.170
The horrors and oddities that D-181 witnessed
during the day always came back to haunt him

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.170
at night.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:24.420
Whether it was a stack of talking bowling
balls attacking him in the grocery store,

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:31.010
or a tea cup that made his skin invert itself
every time he drank it, the SCP objects D-181

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:36.610
worked with always cropped up in his dreams
at night, and they always seemed to be worse.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:42.100
D-181 asked the other D-Class personnel stationed
at the site if they had strange dreams too,

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:45.150
and most of them agreed that they experienced
them as well.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:49.980
Apparently working for the Foundation fired
up the imagination in an extra special way

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:55.580
that seeped into the night time, when D-181
would ideally be receiving some well-deserved

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.050
sleep from the strangeness of the day.

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:02.990
But one dream was bothering D-181 significantly
more than usual.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:07.600
It was a recurring one, happening again and
again every few nights.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.180
The same series of events, playing out over
and over again.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:16.760
The strangest part about it was that it didn’t
feel like a dream at all.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:22.990
D-181 would be laying in his bunk inside Site-32’s
D-Class barracks, desperately trying to fall

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:23.990
asleep.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.870
Eventually he would, but he wouldn’t realize
it.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:33.400
D-181 would feel like he was asleep, but he
could still see the barracks around him, except

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.250
he couldn’t move at all.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:41.780
D-181 was experiencing a form of sleep paralysis,
a phenomenon during falling asleep or waking

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:46.360
up, where a person is unable to move or speak.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:50.780
Hallucinations during sleep paralysis are
common, but the whole experience typically

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.150
only lasts a few minutes.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:58.820
For D-181, it lasted a lot longer, and he
was aware the entire time.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:04.680
So, D-181 would be laying down in his bunk,
trying to fall asleep, when he would suddenly

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.600
become unable to move.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:11.300
Then, from across the room, he’d see the
door to the barracks open up.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:16.540
D-181 knew that the barracks were only accessible
to the upper-ranking personnel, and they never

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.580
came around.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:22.970
First, D-181 saw a large cylinder move itself
slightly into the room.

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:28.030
Then the figure it was attached to waddled
its way through the door - a giant fabric

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:31.890
doll, so big that it could barely fit itself
into the door.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.320
If D-181 could scream, he would.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:42.410
He recognized the figure, an instance of SCP-2386,
one of the anomalies he was working on.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:46.870
The doll walked slow and heavy, trying not
to collapse over its own weight.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:51.820
It was made of pink fabric, with its face
stitched together with thread forming a sly

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:55.190
smile and two buttons for eyes.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:07:00.600
It was terrifying What was even worse were
the two pairs of wings on the dolls back,

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.150
like the kinds you’d see on a butterfly
or a moth.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:08.520
The brilliant patterns looked like they were
made of cloth, sewn to a pair of ordinary

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:12.800
insect wings and completing the doll’s patchwork
appearance.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:18.110
The insect-doll combination stumbled towards
D-181, moving across the barracks slowly and

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:20.500
nearly falling over several times.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:26.970
The creeping terror of the doll’s slow advance
only made D-181 try to move more, but he couldn’t.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:31.910
He was completely paralyzed and subject to
whatever the doll was about to do to him.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:37.120
Eventually, the doll made it close to D-181’s
bunk, standing over the bed and staring at

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:41.070
D-181 with its lifeless, button-eyed face.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.630
It just stood there, staring.

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:47.000
D-181 was sweating, with tears in his eyes.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:51.230
He tried to scream again, but nothing came
out.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:55.940
And then, to make matters worse, the barracks
door opened again, and what made its way through

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:59.060
shook D-181 to his very core.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:04.030
It was another doll, even bigger than the
other one, and behind it was another doll,

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:05.760
and then another.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:11.500
Four dolls in total made their way into the
room and stumbled over to D-181’s bed.

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:16.890
They continued to stare, crowding around the
sleeping D-class like he was a television

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:20.620
set, and their favorite show was about to
begin.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:25.590
Just when D-181 thought it couldn’t get
any worse, the dolls extended their stubby,

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:30.240
felted hands over his face, all four of them
moving in unison.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.330
And then they stopped, and D-181 heard their
voices.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:38.479
Well, not their voices exactly, but voices
nonetheless.

00:08:38.479 --> 00:08:43.620
High-pitched, barely-human, childish voices
started whispering to him.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:49.080
They weren’t coming from the dolls, but
they could talk, D-181 was positive this is

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.190
what they’d sound like.

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:53.580
“You’re doing such a great job.”

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.130
One said.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:59.410
“You’re the Foundation’s greatest asset.”

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:04.100
“We love you, D-181, we love you.”

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:10.250
All of these seemingly innocuous phrases were
things said to D-181 while he was surrounded

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.250
by the giant dolls.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:17.260
On paper, they sound encouraging, but the
context of the situation and the way they

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.900
were said made them anything but.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:25.640
And this would continue for what seemed like
hours, with the dolls crowding D-181 and speaking

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:30.890
to him in his paralyzed state, shouting the
most deceptively kind things possible over

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:36.220
and over again, all while D-181 was aware
the entire time.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:41.030
But before he would wake from this awful dream,
one of the instances would lift their stubby

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:47.110
hand forward, directly hovering over D-181’s
arm and the doll’s appendage would caress

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:51.840
him, squeezing and playing with his arm like
it were a toy.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:57.070
By morning, when D-181 awoke from his dream,
he felt like he was never asleep in the first

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:02.640
place, and that he could remember every agonizing
second of the past night’s experience.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:05.180
This would continue almost every other night.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:09.810
As soon as D-181 would fall asleep, the doll
dream would occur again.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:14.920
As soon as he woke up, he’d feel like he
got next to no sleep the night before.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:20.120
It was draining him, and inhibiting D-181
from performing his duties accordingly.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:24.870
One day during testing, D-181 fell asleep
in the middle of an experiment, and dropped

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:29.360
an important component to the object he was
working with, which nearly set the entire

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:30.730
facility on fire.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:35.080
After that, D-181 knew that something had
to change.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:37.630
D-181 recognized the dolls.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:42.210
They were instances of SCP-2386, which he
had worked with previously.

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:49.550
In fact, it was the experiments with SCP-2386
that injured D-181 on his right arm, causing

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:52.060
an infectious spot to crop up.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:55.660
What caused this, and what exactly is SCP-2386?

00:10:55.660 --> 00:11:01.040
We’ll get to all of that soon enough, but
we need to focus on the dreams.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:06.960
It was three weeks into the dreams, three
weeks since D-181 was injured during testing,

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:10.570
and three weeks since D-181 had a good night’s
sleep.

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:16.970
He met with Dr. Shaw, the head researcher
in charge of SCP-2386 experimentation, and

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:19.810
someone who worked with D-181 many times.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:24.060
Dr. Shaw and D-181 sat down, and prepared
an interview.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.060
She began:

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:27.090
“Good Morning, D-181.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:29.520
You say you've been having recurring dreams?”

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.380
D-181 shuffled in his seat a bit.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.620
“Yeah, hi, doc…

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:35.290
Ever since I got this thing!

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.360
It wasn’t that bad at first.”

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:40.960
D-181, of course, was talking about the red
spot on his arm.

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:45.240
Shaw asked him to explain the dreams, and
D-181 did.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:49.950
He explained how he would be in his bunk,
feeling almost awake but not quite, when giant

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:53.940
versions of SCP-2386 would make their way
into the room.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:59.670
They’d gather around his bed and stare at
him, shouting things, and caressing his infected

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:00.670
spot.

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:03.440
Dr. Shaw listened intently.

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:07.570
D-181 was clearly shaken up from relaying
the experience to another person.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:10.740
He continued, barely able to hold himself
together.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:15.400
You see, something had changed the night before
D-181 spoke to Dr. Shaw.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:19.070
For the first time, the dream was altered.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:22.700
“Actually, last night, they did something
different.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.790
Another one came in.

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.431
It had something with it.

00:12:25.431 --> 00:12:27.330
It looked like a baby one!

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.470
It was all wrapped up in this white cloth.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:33.830
They said something about wanting to show
me what I was working towards…

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:37.670
They pulled back the cloth over its head and
it was a bug's head!

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:38.970
Woke me right the heck up.”

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:44.570
A baby with a bug’s head was definitely
strange imagery, but Dr. Shaw was unsure what

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:45.810
it all could mean.

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:52.221
She knew SCP-2386 were insect-like, and with
the way D-181’s infection was looking, her

00:12:52.221 --> 00:12:56.870
brain began concocting a strange, but potentially
true theory.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:00.029
One that wasn’t looking good for D-181.

00:13:00.029 --> 00:13:04.880
But before we get into that, let’s talk
about what SCP-2386 really is.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:10.090
They’re known among Foundation personnel
at Site-32 as “Pink Ladies”, and they’re

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:15.270
a diminutive species that outwardly resemble
patchwork dolls made of traditional fabric.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:20.520
Think that creepy Raggedy Ann doll your grandmother
has, but ten times more degraded, a whole

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:24.290
lot more pink, and straight up insectoid in
nature.

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:29.540
They’re not as big as the ones in D-181’s
dream, but they’re definitely as scary,

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:33.250
with stitched-on faces and a pair of moth
wings on their backs.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:40.330
In fact, the actual SCP-2386 instances range
from only 7 to 9 centimeters tall.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:47.370
Autopsies on dead instances of SCP-2386 showed
resemblances to human botflies and silkworms,

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:50.990
two species of insects that are absolutely
nasty.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:56.390
It's terrifying to imagine something so outwardly
cuddly could look so downright ugly on the

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:59.050
inside, but that’s what SCP-2386 are.

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:02.130
But don’t try hugging them either.

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:07.380
Their cotton fiber exoskeleton is as durable
as it is gross, and they’re not the kind

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:10.310
of cuddly doll you’d want to take to bed
at night.

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:16.690
In the wild, SCP-2386 are found in hives resembling
similarly patterned seat cushions.

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:21.640
Big mounds of cloth host to tons of these
tiny terrors, with the biggest hive the Foundation

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:24.890
ever came across being the size of a large
sofa.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:30.480
These hives are commonly found near suburban
environments, and sometimes even inside occupied

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:31.800
housing.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:36.480
Imagine coming home to find a brand new sofa
inside your house, and then realizing that

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.400
it's actually home to thousands of SCP-2386
instances.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:47.460
When SCP-2386 leave their colonies, it is
primarily to feed on smaller insects, and

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:50.250
seek out hosts for reproductive purposes.

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:56.170
Despite their cute but gross appearances,
SCP-2386 become hostile if approached by males

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:59.029
of any species, and will target them accordingly.

00:14:59.029 --> 00:15:03.950
That’s why Site-32 only employs male personnel
for testing purposes.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:09.280
As soon as they’re within range of a male
subject, SCP-2386 will outstretch one of its

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:14.840
appendages and extend a pair of scissor-like
claws from it, before swarming the male.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:20.490
This is what happened to D-181, which resulted
in the red, infected spot on his arm.

00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:26.780
Conversely, female subjects in the presence
of SCP-2386 are treated entirely differently,

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:31.570
with the instances caring for them, presenting
them with small gifts, and attempting to play

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:32.830
with them.

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:38.490
During the spring and summer seasons, SCP-2386
will enter their mating season and cease their

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.410
hostilities towards males.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:44.770
Instead, they’ll treat them with the same
level of kindness they do with females.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:47.160
But this kindness is just a front.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:52.850
When given the opportunity, SCP-2386 will
slice a small incision into the male subject,

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:57.770
and pump them full of about 30 to 65 eggs
underneath their skin.

00:15:57.770 --> 00:16:02.940
Within 24 hours, the incised area will resemble
patterned cloth, and genetic tests reveal

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:07.029
it to be composed of the same material as
SCP-2386’s hives.

00:16:07.029 --> 00:16:13.120
In the weeks that follow, this area will spread
across the subject’s body, and eventually,

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:19.960
it will open to reveal fully grown, adult
instances of SCP-2386, who burst from the

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:20.970
patchwork skin.

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:26.280
Dr. Shaw recognized that this is what was
happening to D-181, and immediately got him

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:28.970
to Site-32’s medical ward.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:33.320
D-181 was strapped down to the table, and
tried not to freak out over what he knew was

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.710
about to happen.

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:41.490
The dreams were acting as a warning, and SCP-2386
was clearly looking forward to having D-181

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.390
bear the next generation of insect-dolls.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:48.080
Thankfully, Dr. Shaw caught the infection
before the patchwork skin was able to fully

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:53.300
take root, meaning that the eggs underneath
D-181’s skin were premature.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:55.560
Thankfully, there was still time.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:59.260
Surgery was carried out immediately, and the
doctors weren’t surprised to discover a

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:04.500
colony of premature SCP-2386 eggs underneath
D-181’s arm.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:10.209
They were removed from the body and thrown
into storage for further research purposes.

00:17:10.209 --> 00:17:13.850
D-181, after waking up from the surgery, thanked
Dr. Shaw.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:18.500
At least now he wouldn’t have to deal with
those horrible dreams, and the stinging, swollen

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.829
sensation underneath his arm.

00:17:20.829 --> 00:17:25.370
Unfortunately, he was still a D-Class personnel
working for the Foundation, and would have

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:28.670
many more intense experiences after this one.

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:31.840
But D-181’s gratefulness would soon subside.

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:37.850
Within a few hours, D-181 began to ask Dr.
Shaw if he could see SCP-2386’s enclosure.

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:43.881
He spent the past few weeks absolutely terrified
of the species, but for whatever reason, he

00:17:43.881 --> 00:17:47.000
felt like he had unfinished business with
the anomalies.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.530
He wanted to see them again.

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:54.820
Dr. Shaw became suspicious, and understandably
denied D-181 entrance from the enclosure.

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:56.540
But this wasn’t enough.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:18:01.429
D-181 became violent, and tried to force himself
into the containment chamber.

00:18:01.429 --> 00:18:03.350
He needed to see them!

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.160
He couldn’t explain why, but he felt incomplete.

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:11.160
Eventually, D-181 was subdued and returned
to his quarters, but his symptoms continued

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:12.160
throughout the weeks.

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:18.360
He was depressed, and frequently made reference
to SCP-2386 as being lost, or unrightfully

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.870
taken away from him.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:22.530
To Dr. Shaw, what happened was clear.

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:28.520
D-181 had been affected mentally upon receiving
the SCP-2386 eggs.

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:33.500
This was a safety mechanism induced by the
anomaly in the case of birthing complications,

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:38.800
so D-181 would feel compelled to receive another
batch of eggs into his body if the first batch

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:40.730
was lost or damaged.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:46.450
It was disgusting, and Shaw was positive it
would subside after a few more weeks, but

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:52.980
what kept her up at night wasn’t the same
dreams D-181 had, or the terror of SCP-2386.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:59.930
It was the image of D-181, scared and out
of his mind, clawing that containment chamber

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:07.500
door, begging to be used as a host for SCP-2386’s
next batch of eggs.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:13.941
Now go check out “SCP-3004 - Insect God
- Imago” and “SCP-439 - Bone Hive” for

00:19:13.941 --> 00:19:17.370
more anomalous SCP Explained videos that will
bug you out!

